          rows={[["Where it sits", "On the wellhead or casing head below the rig floor (surface stack), or latched to the subsea wellhead on the seabed (subsea stack)."], ["Common bore sizes", "7-1/16\", 11\", 13-5/8\", 18-3/4\" and 21-1/4\" nominal through-bore; 13-5/8\" is the most common land and platform size, 18-3/4\" the usual subsea size."], ["Working pressure classes", "2,000, 3,000, 5,000, 10,000, 15,000 and 20,000 psi (2M–20M)."], ["Sealing elements", "Annular preventer (elastomer packing unit); ram preventers fitted with pipe, variable bore, blind, blind shear or casing shear rams."], ["Elastomers", "Nitrile (NBR) for general service; hydrogenated nitrile (HNBR) and specialist compounds for higher temperature or sour service."], ["Operated by", "Hydraulic fluid stored in nitrogen-precharged accumulator bottles, typically a 3,000 psi closing system on surface stacks."]]}
